/*
:name: tuple_literal_absent_field
:type: error
:error: unknown field `r` on the tuple expression
:help: tuple expression has fields: p, q.*has 'r'
*/
// A field read on an inline tuple literal whose name is absent is a compile
// error (03-bundle.md). The source of the read is a compiler temp, but it is
// NOT a call result: the diagnostic must not call it "the call result" nor
// suggest a destructure `slot=field` rename (there is no call and no
// destructure here). Only a temp recorded as a call result
// (destructure_callee_slot_mismatch.prp) gets the call wording.
pub mod tuple_literal_absent_field(a:U8) -> (z:U8@[0]) {
  z = (const p = a, const q = 3).r  // locate_error_here
}
